---
layout: null
---
{%- comment -%}
  The client-side search index. Every post, as plain text.

  `plain_text` is _plugins/search_index.rb rather than `strip_html |
  strip_newlines`: it decodes HTML entities (kramdown escapes a literal `>` to
  `&gt;`) and leaves a space at block boundaries, so `<p>끝</p><p>시작</p>` is two
  words, not one.

  There is no `snippet` field: js/search.js cuts the shown excerpt around the
  match in `content`.

  js/search.js matches a query against title, tags, category and content, and
  ranks by which of them hold it; `translation` makes a pair count once.
{%- endcomment -%}
[
  {% for post in site.posts %}
    {
      "title": {{ post.title | jsonify }},
      "url": "{{ site.baseurl }}{{ post.url }}",
      "date": "{{ post.posted_at | date: site.date_format }}",
      "lang": {{ post.lang | default: site.lang | jsonify }},
      "translation": {{ post.translation_id | jsonify }},
      "category": {{ post.categories | join: ', ' | replace: '-', ' ' | jsonify }},
      "tags": {{ post.tags | join: ', ' | replace: '-', ' ' | jsonify }},
      "content": {{ post.content | plain_text | jsonify }}
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
]
